.TH "PB-CONFIG-LOCAL-ACCESS-DOMAIN" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-config-local-access-domain - Set the local browser domain


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb config local-access domain [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Choose the DNS domain used for this user's local browser URLs. Changing the domain provisions local trust through the normal privileged installation path and updates the daemon before this command reports success.

.PP
With --json, this command group lists its available commands.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for domain


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-config-local-access(1)\fP, \fBpb-config-local-access-domain-reset(1)\fP, \fBpb-config-local-access-domain-set(1)\fP
